NNAAMMEE
     zzppooooll--iinniittiiaalliizzee — write to unallocated regions of ZFS storage pool

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     zzppooooll iinniittiiaalliizzee [--cc|--ss |--uu] [--ww] _p_o_o_l [_d_e_v_i_c_e]â¦

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     Begins initializing by writing to all unallocated regions on the speci‐
     fied devices, or all eligible devices in the pool if no individual de‐
     vices are specified.  Only leaf data or log devices may be initialized.

     --cc, ----ccaanncceell
             Cancel initializing on the specified devices, or all eligible de‐
             vices if none are specified.  If one or more target devices are
             invalid or are not currently being initialized, the command will
             fail and no cancellation will occur on any device.

     --ss, ----ssuussppeenndd
             Suspend initializing on the specified devices, or all eligible
             devices if none are specified.  If one or more target devices are
             invalid or are not currently being initialized, the command will
             fail and no suspension will occur on any device.  Initializing
             can then be resumed by running zzppooooll iinniittiiaalliizzee with no flags on
             the relevant target devices.

     --uu, ----uunniinniitt
             Clears the initialization state on the specified devices, or all
             eligible devices if none are specified.  If the devices are being
             actively initialized the command will fail.  After being cleared
             zzppooooll iinniittiiaalliizzee with no flags can be used to re-initialize all
             unallocoated regions on the relevant target devices.

     --ww, ----wwaaiitt
             Wait until the devices have finished initializing before return‐
             ing.

